# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this React application using the latest official documentation from Vercel.

## What Was Implemented

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package version 2.0.0 using npm
- Package manager: npm (as indicated by package-lock.json)

### 2. Code Changes

#### Modified Files:
- **package.json**: Added `@vercel/speed-insights` dependency
- **package-lock.json**: Updated with new dependency tree
- **src/App.jsx**: Integrated SpeedInsights component

#### Implementation Details:
Following the official Vercel documentation for React applications, I:

1. **Added the import statement** in `src/App.jsx`:
   ```jsx
   import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/react";
   ```

2. **Placed the SpeedInsights component** in the App component:
   - Added `<SpeedInsights />` right after the `<Toaster />` component
   - Positioned inside the `<ErrorBoundary>` wrapper to ensure proper error handling
   - Placed before the `<Router>` to ensure it tracks all routes

This placement ensures that Speed Insights will track all pages and user interactions throughout the application.

### 3. Verification Steps Completed

✅ **Build Test**: Successfully built the project with `npm run build`
   - No errors introduced
   - Build completed in 1.10s
   - All chunks generated correctly

✅ **Linting**: Ran `npm run lint` with oxlint
   - No new errors introduced
   - 18 pre-existing warnings (unrelated to our changes)
   - All warnings are from other parts of the codebase

✅ **Git Staging**: All changes properly staged
   - package.json
   - package-lock.json
   - src/App.jsx

## Framework Information
- **Framework**: React with Vite
- **React Version**: 19.2.7
- **Build Tool**: Vite 8.1.1

## Next Steps for User

After this PR is merged and deployed to Vercel:

1. **Enable Speed Insights** in the Vercel dashboard:
   - Navigate to your project in Vercel
   - Go to Speed Insights from the sidebar
   - Click the "Enable" button

2. **Monitor Performance**: 
   - Data will start collecting after deployment
   - Metrics will become visible in the dashboard after several days of traffic
   - Access insights at: Vercel Dashboard > Your Project > Speed Insights

## Technical Notes

- The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for React applications
- The SpeedInsights component is a zero-config component that automatically tracks Web Vitals
- No additional configuration is required for basic functionality
- The component is lightweight and won't impact application performance
- It works on all Vercel plans (including free tier)

## References
- Official Documentation: https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- Package: @vercel/speed-insights v2.0.0
